    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `api/owners.POST.yml` (15 steps). Everything from step 5 onward runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n## Precondition\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the file is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request never enters the pipeline.\n\n## 1. `RequireOwnerFields` \u2014 validate\n- **Side-effect:** normalises `address` via `NormaliseAddress` (trim, collapse internal whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST\u2192STREET`/`RD\u2192ROAD`/`AVE\u2192AVENUE`) and writes it back onto the request. A null/blank address becomes `\"\"`.\n- **Validation:** `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must all be non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400) listing the missing fields.\n- **Side-effect:** normalises `telephone` to E.164 (`E164Telephone`: strip separators, keep/assume `+61`, drop a leading `0`, enforce digit-length rules) and writes it back.\n- **Validation:** if the telephone can't be formed into valid E.164 \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException([\"telephone\"])` (400).\n- **Side-effect:** publishes the validated body as `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>` for all later steps.\n\n## 2. `RequireCurrentRegistrationDate`\n- **Validation:** if `registrationDate` is supplied and is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Absent date is left alone.\n\n## 3. `RequirePostcode`\n- **Validation:** if `postcode` is present it must be exactly 4 digits; and for a city with a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in that range \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Absent postcode, or a city with no known region, is accepted.\n\n## 4. `NormaliseEmail`\n- **Validation:** if `email` is present it must match the email regex and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException([\"email\"])` (400).\n- **Side-effect:** lower-cases the email and writes it back. Absent email is left alone.\n\n## 5. `RequireUniqueIdentity` *(transaction starts)*\n- **Validation:** scans `ownerRepository.findAll()`; if any existing owner has the same (E.164-normalised) telephone \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException`. This is the only hard duplicate check (telephone-based).\n\n## 6. `RequireUniqueHousehold`\n- **Validation:** skipped if `sharesHousehold == true` or postcode is blank. Otherwise derives `HouseholdId` (SHA-256 of normalised lastName + `|` + postcode); if any existing owner resolves to the same household id \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException`.\n\n## 7. `RequireCityCapacity`\n- **Validation:** counts existing owners with an exactly-matching `city`; if `>= 50` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n## 8. `RequireDailyCapacity`\n- **Validation:** computes the day = `BusinessDay.roll(registrationDate or today)`; counts existing owners registered on that day; if `>= 100` \u2192 `DailyLimitException`.\n\n## 9. `BuildOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** maps `OwnerFieldsDto` \u2192 `Owner` via `OwnerMapper` (`id` and `pets` ignored).\n- **Side-effect:** sets `registrationDate = BusinessDay.roll(registrationDate or today)` \u2014 a weekend date rolls forward to Monday.\n\n## 10. `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from postcode/city (`Locality`) and HASH8 is the first 8 uppercase hex chars of SHA-256 over `E.164-telephone + lastName`.\n\n## 11. `CountNamesakes`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing the same `HouseholdId` (lastName + postcode). (Feeds membership scoring later.)\n\n## 12. `DetectPossibleDuplicate`\n- **Side-effect:** skipped if `sharesHousehold == true` or no postcode. Otherwise finds an existing owner in the same household but with a *different* telephone and records its id in `possibleDuplicateOf` (surfaced as `possibleDuplicate` in the response).\n\n## 13. `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists the owner and assigns its id.\n- **Side-effect:** writes an `AUDIT` log line (`Created owner id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026`).\n\n## 14. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** maps the saved `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`; the mapper computes derived fields: `telephoneDisplay`, `displayName`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel` (from `namesakeCount` + email + tenure via `MembershipTier`), `locality`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`, and `possibleDuplicate`.\n- **Side-effect:** sets `bulkSignupWarning` = `BulkSignup.warningToday(...)` (true when > 80 owners already created today).\n- **Side-effect:** responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n- The governed transaction commits at the end of the pipeline.\n\n---\n\nWorth flagging: the codebase also contains `ValidateOwner`, `RequireUniqueEmail`, and `RequireUniqueTelephone`, but **none of them are referenced by `owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 this endpoint's uniqueness check is `RequireUniqueIdentity` (telephone-only), not the separate email/telephone checks."
